From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:35:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2: keep the 10 bits of a stream for an encoder that reads
 the decoder's Surface

A client that renders to a Surface makes the framework set the decoder's pixel
format to IMPLEMENTATION_DEFINED. The decoder listed no such value, so the
setter refused it and the format stayed at 8-bit YUV 4:2:0: a Main 10 stream
decoded onto the input Surface of a video encoder (a transcode, and CTS
CodecEncoderSurfaceTest) reached a Main 10 encoder as 8-bit NV12.

List IMPLEMENTATION_DEFINED, and take the usage of the Surface's consumer
(C2_PARAMKEY_OUTPUT_STREAM_USAGE, which the framework sets from the Surface).
When the consumer is a video encoder the decoder asks the device for P010 if
the device describes the stream as P010: TRY_FMT refuses it for a stream with
8-bit samples, which keeps the layout the device chose. Any other Surface, a
display, still gets 8-bit samples, since the host cannot show P010. The
decoder reads the client's format at every resolution change, because the
usage arrives after the decoder starts. V4L2Queue::tryFormat's refusal is a
probe, so it is logged at debug level.
---
